---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/alternatives/yotpo-email-sms-alternative';
const title = 'Yotpo Email & SMS alternatives: choose a replacement for Shopify';
const desc = 'Compare replacement messaging around retained Reviews and Loyalty, demonstrate critical workflows, and cost the new stack after Yotpo Email and SMS retirement.';
const faqs = [
  { question: 'Can I stay on Yotpo Email & SMS?', answer: 'Yotpo scheduled full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Its current notice confirms the SMS dashboard and background services are inactive. Choose a current sending destination; continuing Reviews or Loyalty does not restore messaging.' },
  { question: 'Which replacements did Yotpo name?', answer: 'Yotpo named Attentive and Omnisend in its 2025 migration announcement. Treat these as vendor-recommended candidates, then verify current onboarding, scope and commercial terms. The announcement is not an independent ranking.' },
  { question: 'Must I move Reviews too?', answer: 'No. Decide whether Reviews still serves your store separately. If retaining it, validate product matching, review data and request ownership in the new sender. If moving it, evaluate asset rights and historical review transfer as a separate project.' },
  { question: 'Will loyalty points survive a sender change?', answer: 'Keeping Loyalty leaves its program as the source of reward rules. Demonstrate balance, tier, redemption and expiry data in the destination; confirm freshness and cancellation behavior. A contact import alone does not reproduce these workflows.' },
  { question: 'Is there a cheapest replacement?', answer: 'Compare written quotes at the same contact count, email volume, SMS destinations and segments, retained modules and support workload. Include integration labor and contract overlap. Old Yotpo module estimates cannot price a current replacement.' },
  { question: 'Can I still export from the old dashboard?', answer: 'The current SMS notice says dashboard access is inactive. Start with archived exports and existing destination records, ask support what recovery is possible, and document missing data. Do not promise an export or import records with unresolved sending eligibility.' },
  { question: 'Should email and SMS move together?', answer: 'Choose one or two senders according to your operating needs. Separate senders require a demonstrated shared preference process, purchase cancellation and reply ownership. A single vendor still needs these checks across its channels.' },
  { question: 'How long should replacement take?', answer: 'Use readiness gates rather than a fixed timeline. Activate only after sender setup, permission and suppression reconciliation, event mapping, module-data checks and cancellation tests pass. Confirm any migration assistance and availability in writing.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/alternatives">← Alternatives</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Replacement selection · checked November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Choose a replacement for retired Yotpo Email &amp; SMS</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">The decision is which platform should now send your messages and which Yotpo module data it needs. Keeping Reviews or Loyalty can be sensible without recreating the former suite. Start from required workflows and a demonstrable handoff, rather than an eight-vendor ranking.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Start with the retirement and the two named partners</h2>
      <p>Yotpo's <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">migration announcement</a> scheduled full Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025 and named Attentive and Omnisend as partners. Its <a class="link" href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">current notice</a> confirms inactive SMS dashboard and background services. This replaces the old choice to keep buying the messaging suite; it does not require replacing Reviews and Loyalty.</p>
      <p>Yotpo documents <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/integrations/attentive/">Attentive review and loyalty data synchronization</a> and <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/integrations/omnisend/">Omnisend segmentation using Yotpo data</a>. Those are concrete reasons to include them in a shortlist when retaining modules. They do not guarantee every account's field coverage, migration access or promotional pricing.</p>
      <p>Request a demonstration using your actual data contract: identity key, fields, triggering event, update interval and failure handling. Confirm Reviews and Loyalty separately. For supplier history and archived SMS records, use the <a class="link" href="/apps/smsbump">SMSBump continuity guide</a>; for the full retirement inventory see <a class="link" href="/apps/yotpo-email-sms">Yotpo Email &amp; SMS</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8 overflow-x-auto">
      <h2>Shortlist by the destination's job</h2>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Store requirement</th><th>Selection route</th><th>Evidence to request</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Keep Reviews and Loyalty; use their data in messaging</td><td>Begin with named partners Attentive and Omnisend</td><td>Live field mapping and event demonstration for each retained module, plus plan access and failure alerts</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Keep an established email sender; replace SMS</td><td>Evaluate a current SMS supplier such as Postscript alongside the existing email owner</td><td>Destination coverage, number handoff, reply staffing, suppression propagation and purchase cancellation across senders</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Replace email and SMS under one operator</td><td>Compare a unified proposal with the cost of two coordinated senders</td><td>Both channels' required flows, audience limits, approval process and billing units on a matched workload</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Move Reviews or Loyalty as well</td><td>Run a separate module selection before promising full suite transfer</td><td>Review rights and product mapping, or rewards balances and redemption rules, with reconciliation totals</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript guide</a> covers a current SMS-focused operating decision. Existing email candidates such as <a class="link" href="/apps/sequenzy">Sequenzy</a> and <a class="link" href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo</a> belong in your comparison when they meet the email brief; neither is declared the winner here. Require direct proof of any Yotpo data bridge you need. Do not buy a loyalty or popup product merely to fill a slot in an alternative list.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Use the same demonstration brief for every candidate</h2>
      <p>Prepare test profiles and a small set of known orders. These are proposed acceptance exercises, with no measured merchant results or setup-speed advantage claimed.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Beauty with Reviews:</strong> match a review to the right product and show usable content with the necessary rights. Trigger one post-delivery request, then demonstrate that a completed review or the other request owner prevents a duplicate. A generic product-rating block does not prove request orchestration.</li>
        <li><strong>Loyalty-led retail:</strong> show a tier change, points redemption and an expiry reminder. Change the balance after scheduling and inspect the final message. Reject a stale reward promise even if the template looks correct.</li>
        <li><strong>Apparel replies:</strong> route a sizing question to a staffed inbox, retain the order context and handle an opt-out. Ask who monitors failures outside campaign hours; a reply feature without an owner does not meet a support requirement.</li>
        <li><strong>Cart across channels:</strong> queue email and SMS, then purchase and withdraw permission on separate test profiles. Check each cancellation and replay the event to expose duplicate jobs. An unopened email must not supply SMS eligibility.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Record pass, fail or unavailable with the account configuration and evidence. A missed critical cancellation or unusable permission record blocks that workflow. Nice-to-have templates should not outweigh a failed mandatory requirement.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Compare complete quotes, then assign the handoff</h2>
      <p>Give candidates the same active profile count, email sends, SMS destinations, expected segments and peak-month scenario. Ask for platform charges, carrier fees, support scope, implementation cost and minimum term. Keep retained Reviews and Loyalty contracts on separate lines so their cost is not mistaken for messaging savings.</p>
      <p><strong>Illustrative workload, not a supplier quote:</strong> four campaigns to 5,000 eligible email profiles plus 3,000 automation emails means 23,000 emails. A peak month with another 2,000 sends means 25,000. Quote SMS separately using actual encoding and segment counts rather than assuming one recipient equals one billable segment. Add staff hours for replies and integration monitoring to each proposal.</p>
      <p>Inventory any replacement already installed before importing again. Reconcile archived permission and withdrawal records, document unavailable old records, verify domain and sender setup, map events and appoint one owner per flow. Turn off replaced integrations and queues before activating the new owner. Ask support about recovery where the decommissioned dashboard prevents access.</p>
      <p>Accept the destination when required demonstrations pass and the team can handle failures. After launch compare delivery failures, complaints, reply backlog and contribution with a documented baseline. Use a suitable eligible comparison group when estimating incremental gains. No fixed migration duration, price saving or revenue lift follows from switching suppliers alone.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Yotpo replacement selection FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
